                <pb facs="1016" n="912" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg912"/>

                <head>Case of Miguel Diego at Las Vacas.</head>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summary.</hi>—Upon complaint of H. J. Ware, that
                    Diego’s store had been looted by federal troops, the Consul at Ciudad Porfirio
                    Díaz was instructed to endeavor to secure the return of the stolen goods. Upon
                    protest by the Consul, the federal general at C. P. Díaz telegraphed December 4
                    to the local commander at Las Vacas to return the property and not to molest
                    foreigners in the future. (File Nos. 312.51/48, 49, 52, 69.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
